Before inferring an ARC transformation, compare input and demonstration-output dimensions. A smaller output is a strong signal that the task may extract or encode a property, rather than paint a full-size grid. Do not assume a template-stamping task solely because the input contains separators, repeating blocks, or sparse colored markers.

